  "title": "Meta and Social Media Companies Face Legal Battles Over Child Safety",
  "summary": "A closely watched social media addiction lawsuit against Meta was dropped after the plaintiff voluntarily dismissed his claims against Meta, leaving none of the major tech companies facing trial in the case. France has passed a law banning social media access for under-15s, and a New Mexico judge ordered the Instagram, Facebook, and WhatsApp parent company to pay another $567m for the way it has harmed children.",
  "facts": [
